  "id": "20260918-v3-stage-cp07c-engine-in-v3",
  "title": "V3 stage-oriented refactor CP07c — move the generic engine into V3 with its hybrid trust contract",
  "goal": "Move the generic Architecture Conformance engine into docs/guards/V3/stages/post/gates/architecture/dotnet, write the hybrid trust contract of section 11.3 and prove that the composite policy hash, the report fields, the failure categories and the v3-architecture check name are unchanged (P6.4, P6.5, P6.6, D29).",
  "acceptanceCriteria": [
    "The engine sources, project and assembly live in V3 as Guards.ArchitectureConformance, the IFX binding and host reference that project, and V3_ifx keeps only policy, baseline, binding and IFX fixtures.",
    "The v3-architecture trust contract states the policy binding, the blind spots and which required check cross-covers each one, and the stage schema and monotonicity declarations cover the new fields.",
    "The composite policy hash matches the reviewed baseline, the report fields, the twelve policy bindings, the tool version and the check names are unchanged, the 184 engine and 10 IFX binding tests pass, and all 13 required checks pass."
  ],
